{"ok":true,"schema":"figure-series-descriptions@1","key":"FIG-30f0e8615f733499","lines":["### 1. Diagrammtyp & Architektur-Kontext","UML-Klassendiagramm zur Spezifikation von Service-Instanzen und deren Service-Discovery-Konfiguration (SOME/IP-SD) im AUTOSAR-System-Template (E/E-Architektur und serviceorientierte Kommunikation).","","### 2. Komponenten, Entitäten & Schnittstellen","- `ApplicationEndpoint` (spezialisiert `Identifiable`):","  - Attribut: `priority :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","  - Kompositionen:","    - `+providedServiceInstance` (Kardinalität `0..*`) zu `ProvidedServiceInstance`","    - `+consumedServiceInstance` (Kardinalität `0..*`) zu `ConsumedServiceInstance`","- `AbstractServiceInstance` (spezialisiert `Identifiable`):","  - Generalisierung für `ProvidedServiceInstance` und `ConsumedServiceInstance` (Subklassen erben via Vererbungspfeil `+serviceInstance 0..*`)","- `DataMapping`:","  - Attribut: `communicationDirection :CommunicationDirectionType [0..1]`","  - Assoziiert mit `AbstractServiceInstance`","- `ProvidedServiceInstance`:","  - Attribute:","    - `instanceIdentifier :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `priority :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `serviceIdentifier :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","  - Komposition: `+sdServerConfig` (Kardinalität `0..1`) zu `SdServerConfig`","  - Assoziation: `+providedServiceInstance` (Kardinalität `1`) ausgehend von `ConsumedServiceInstance`","- `ConsumedServiceInstance`:","  - Komposition: `+sdClientConfig` (Kardinalität `0..1`) zu `SdClientConfig`","  - Referenziert genau eine `ProvidedServiceInstance` via `+providedServiceInstance 1`","- `SdServerConfig`:","    - `offerCyclicDelay :TimeValue [0..1]`","    - `serverServiceMajorVersion :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `serverServiceMinorVersion :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `ttl :PositiveInteger`","    - `+requestResponseDelay` (Kardinalität `0..1`) zu `RequestResponseDelay`","    - `+capabilityRecord` (Kardinalität `0..*`) zu `TagWithOptionalValue`","    - `+initialOfferBehavior` (Kardinalität `0..1`) zu `InitialSdDelayConfig`","- `SdClientConfig`:","    - `clientServiceMajorVersion :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `clientServiceMinorVersion :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `+initialFindBehavior` (Kardinalität `0..1`) zu `InitialSdDelayConfig`","- `TagWithOptionalValue`:","    - `key :String`","    - `value :String [0..1]`","- `RequestResponseDelay`:","    - `maxValue :TimeValue`","    - `minValue :TimeValue`","- `InitialSdDelayConfig`:","    - `initialDelayMaxValue :TimeValue`","    - `initialDelayMinValue :TimeValue`","    - `initialRepetitionsBaseDelay :TimeValue [0..1]`","    - `initialRepetitionsMax :PositiveInteger [0..1]`","### 3. Dynamisches Verhalten & Sequenzablauf","Statisches Metamodell ohne Verhaltens- oder Sequenzdiagrammelemente. Es definiert Konfigurationsstrukturen für dynamische Service-Discovery-Prozesse:","- Ein Server bietet Service-Instanzen zyklisch (`offerCyclicDelay`) oder mit Initialverzögerung (`initialOfferBehavior`) via SOME/IP Offer-Service-Nachrichten an.","- Ein Client sucht Instanzen mit gesteuertem Suchverhalten (`initialFindBehavior`) via Find-Service-Nachrichten.","- Antwortzeiten auf Discovery-Anfragen werden über Minimal- und Maximalverzögerungen (`RequestResponseDelay`) eingegrenzt.","- Dienstgültigkeitsdauern werden über Time-to-Live (`ttl`) festgelegt.","### 4. Normative Relevanz & Entwickler-Hinweise","- Ein `ApplicationEndpoint` kapselt beliebig viele bereitgestellte und konsumierte Service-Instanzen eines Netzwerk-Endpunkts.","- Jede `ConsumedServiceInstance` erfordert zwingend die Zuordnung zu genau einer `ProvidedServiceInstance` (`+providedServiceInstance 1`).","- Instanz- und Service-Identifikatoren (`serviceIdentifier`, `instanceIdentifier`) sowie Major- und Minor-Versionen müssen sender- und empfängerseitig kompatibel konfiguriert sein.","- `ttl` ist in `SdServerConfig` und `SdClientConfig` ein Pflichtattribut (Kardinalität 1).","- Zeitwerte (`TimeValue`) in Verzögerungskonfigurationen steuern das Sendezeitraster und Jitter-Verhalten auf dem Bus.","  - Attribut: `priority: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","  - Attribut: `communicationDirection: CommunicationDirectionType [0..1]`","    - `instanceIdentifier: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `loadBalancingPriority: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `loadBalancingWeight: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `priority: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `serviceIdentifier: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `offerCyclicDelay: TimeValue [0..1]`","    - `serverServiceMajorVersion: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `serverServiceMinorVersion: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `ttl: PositiveInteger`","    - `clientServiceMajorVersion: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `clientServiceMinorVersion: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","    - `key: String`","    - `value: String [0..1]`","    - `maxValue: TimeValue`","    - `minValue: TimeValue`","    - `initialDelayMaxValue: TimeValue`","    - `initialDelayMinValue: TimeValue`","    - `initialRepetitionsBaseDelay: TimeValue [0..1]`","    - `initialRepetitionsMax: PositiveInteger [0..1]`","- `ProvidedServiceInstance` bietet mit `loadBalancingPriority` und `loadBalancingWeight` Mechanismen zur Lastverteilung zwischen redundanten Server-Instanzen desselben Dienstes."],"versions":[{"id":"FIG-30f0e8615f733499","releases":["R4.1.3"],"l":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,2,9,10,2,11,12,13,2,14,15,16,17,18,19,20,2,21,22,23,2,24,15,25,26,27,28,6,29,30,31,2,32,15,33,34,28,6,30,35,29,2,36,15,37,38,2,39,15,40,41,2,42,15,43,44,45,46,2,47,48,49,50,51,52,2,53,54,55,56,57,58,2],"model":"gemini-3.8-flash (via agy)","at":"2026-10-08","recipe":"figure-series@1"},{"id":"FIG-86d8a62143852e92","releases":["R4.2.2"],"l":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,2,9,10,2,11,12,13,2,14,15,16,17,18,19,20,2,21,22,23,2,24,15,25,26,27,28,6,29,30,31,2,32,15,33,34,28,6,30,35,29,2,36,15,37,38,2,39,15,40,41,2,42,15,43,44,45,46,2,47,48,49,50,51,52,2,53,54,55,56,57,58,2],"model":"gemini-3.8-flash (via agy)","at":"2026-10-08","recipe":"figure-series@1"},{"i